      "edition": "simplified",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
        "no_added_claims": false,
        "names_and_negations": true,
        "speaker_attribution": true,
        "source_choices_and_notes": false,
        "terminology_policy": true
      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ πάντοτε σπλάγχνον ἔχοντες ἐπὶ πάντα ἄνθρωπον",
          "english_quote": "They had compassion for everyone.",
          "issue": "The independently repeated πάντοτε, “always,” is omitted from the compassion clause. Earlier occurrences of “always” qualify other predicates and do not explicitly preserve this clause's emphasis.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “They always had compassion for everyone,” subject to fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἐπλήθυνεν αὐτοὺς ἐν τοῖς κόποις τῶν χειρῶν αὐτῶν",
          "english_quote": "He made their work prosper",
          "issue": "The simplification drops “of their hands,” replacing the source's concrete description of their labor with unrestricted “work.”",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider “He made them prosper in the work of their hands,” subject to fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "καὶ ἐνδεδυμένοι ⸢τὸ⸣ πνεῦμα ⸢τὸ ἅγιον⸣ τούτων τῶν παρθένων",
          "english_quote": "The house/clothing and virgins imagery is retained;",
          "issue": "The note claims retention of house imagery that is absent from the selected source. The simplified edition inherits this unsupported description independently of its otherwise faithful clothing clause.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace this clause with “The clothing and virgins imagery is retained.” Identify and substantiate any broader contextual reference separately; review the replacement before acceptance.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "λέγω δὲ ὑμῖν τοῖς τοιούτοις οὖσιν ἐγὼ ὁ ἄγγελος τῆς μετανοίας· διαμείνατε τοιοῦτοι, καὶ οὐκ ἐξαλειφθήσεται τὸ σπέρμα ὑμῶν ἕως αἰῶνος.",
          "english_quote": "Preserve repentance conditions, confession, mercy and healing, and the declared foolishness, childlikeness/gentleness and spirit/seed alternatives.",
          "issue": "The unit-specific simplification metadata claims preservation of confession, mercy, healing, and a foolishness alternative, none of which occurs in this selected unit. The supplied report locates the foolishness alternative in S.9.xxii.4, not S.9.xxiv.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace the inherited metadata with an accurate account of this unit's simplification, addressing its exhortation to remain as described, offspring promise, and disclosed childlikeness/gentleness and spirit/seed alternatives. Review the replacement independently.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions require revision. The standard text covers the selected clauses, but its imagery note adds an unsupported description. The simplified edition additionally omits explicit wording and contains mis-scoped simplification metadata. Both preserve reader-facing “servants,” contextual “repentance,” speaker identity, and the strong offspring promises. The disclosed childlikeness and spirit working readings remain source-compatible; their alternatives and conjectural status agree with the supplied project report. This review does not authenticate unseen manuscripts or certify exhaustive collation. Proposed corrections require fresh review."
